WEBVTT

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:26.750
Sudha…

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:42.542
Mom.

00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:49.958
Would you like some <i>poha?</i>

00:00:50.042 --> 00:00:51.500
- Will you make it?
- Yes.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.125
Yes, of course.

00:00:58.542 --> 00:00:59.708
Yes, Mom. Namaste.

00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:03.583
I'm doing great. How are you?

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.583
No, I just got back this morning.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.875
There was an urgent meeting
at the head office.

00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:10.875
That's why.

00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:13.292
Yes?

00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:16.583
No, I'm just about to leave. And Dad?

00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:28.458
Chander, where's the cumin?

00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:30.708
Oh, found it!

00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:39.292
Mom, I'm getting an urgent call.
I'll call you back later. Okay?

00:02:34.958 --> 00:02:39.583
{\an8}GARGI:
SUDHA, WHERE ARE YOU? PLEASE CALL ME

00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:03.417
Super Attorney Sudha Tripathi
starts her day with the Bollywood section.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.833
Why? Don't you read it?

00:03:06.375 --> 00:03:09.208
I find these Bollywood people
to be very shallow.

00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:11.708
And their news is just as useless.

00:03:11.792 --> 00:03:12.792
What do you think?

00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:17.458
The rest of the newspaper
has very serious journalism?

00:03:17.542 --> 00:03:20.542
If everything's fake, why do you bother
with the Bollywood section?

00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:23.167
Because at least the people
look beautiful in the photos.

00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:43.583
Wanna try?

00:03:45.292 --> 00:03:46.208
Okay.

00:03:47.625 --> 00:03:51.000
So, after grinding the coffee,
we'll start by lighting the siphon.

00:03:52.292 --> 00:03:53.417
And then?

00:04:02.292 --> 00:04:03.292
And then?

00:04:04.292 --> 00:04:08.125
After that, we'll give the coffee
another quick grind.

00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:12.083
That's it.

00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:18.000
Thank you.

00:04:27.083 --> 00:04:28.125
So much effort?

00:04:29.417 --> 00:04:31.333
You need to give the coffee some time.

00:04:33.542 --> 00:04:34.500
With patience.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.500
My patience runs thin.

00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:41.208
So, I prefer tea.

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:45.125
I can teach you, if you want.

00:04:47.042 --> 00:04:47.958
Patience.

00:04:50.875 --> 00:04:52.292
Oh!

00:04:56.792 --> 00:04:58.917
- I'm really sorry. I was--
- No.

00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:01.000
It's not your fault.

00:05:03.208 --> 00:05:04.292
Taste the <i>poha.</i>

00:05:08.375 --> 00:05:10.375
Aren't you getting late for work?

00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:11.917
I don't feel like going to work today.

00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:15.042
What's going on, Chander Sharma?

00:05:15.583 --> 00:05:16.458
Tell me.

00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:19.708
Today…

00:05:21.375 --> 00:05:23.000
the <i>poha </i>turned out really good.

00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:28.125
Just tell me the truth.

00:05:29.042 --> 00:05:33.042
"Sudha, I don't feel like
going to work today because of you."

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.958
- I wanted to say that, but…
- This!

00:05:39.042 --> 00:05:41.708
This is exactly India's problem!

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.042
Ninety percent of boys
lose their chance at "but."

00:05:46.542 --> 00:05:48.042
Here's the golden rule of my life.

00:05:48.125 --> 00:05:50.333
Whenever you're confused
and find yourself thinking,

00:05:50.417 --> 00:05:53.458
"Should I do it or not?
Should I say it or not?"

00:05:53.542 --> 00:05:57.333
Just go for it.
Say it without overthinking it.

00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:00.000
What even are you?

00:06:07.292 --> 00:06:08.417
By the way,

00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:11.875
Gargi, my roommate,
has been messaging me repeatedly.

00:06:11.958 --> 00:06:13.583
She really wants me to come back.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:26.125
But I was thinking that
if I stay here for a few more days…

00:06:30.042 --> 00:06:32.083
It's not like
I'm throwing you out of the house.

00:06:33.708 --> 00:06:34.583
Okay.

00:06:35.292 --> 00:06:37.167
I have to get ready for court.

00:06:38.417 --> 00:06:39.833
I will see you later?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:47.667
Well, I'm thinking
I should go to the office.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:55.875
Hello.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.375
Gargi?

00:07:04.458 --> 00:07:05.333
Sudha?

00:07:06.083 --> 00:07:08.583
- What's the update on your hearing?
- There's still some time.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.958
But the case closes today, so we're good.

00:07:12.208 --> 00:07:13.375
That's why I'm here.

00:07:13.458 --> 00:07:16.792
To make peace with you, Sudha, over tea.

00:07:18.083 --> 00:07:19.167
Fine.

00:07:25.458 --> 00:07:26.333
What's going on?

00:07:26.958 --> 00:07:28.708
- Something is different today.
- Yes!

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.417
What is this?

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:39.292
I got an offer letter from a big firm
in Mumbai. Litigation cases.

00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:42.292
Oh my God! When do you join?
And package?

00:07:42.375 --> 00:07:43.792
But, Sudha…

00:07:44.667 --> 00:07:46.458
I haven't accepted the offer yet.

00:07:46.542 --> 00:07:48.292
This is Mumbai High Court
we're talking about.

00:07:48.375 --> 00:07:50.958
- I know!
- So, what are you waiting for?

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:54.375
Because right now, it's tea
in Bhopal that I like more.

00:08:08.375 --> 00:08:09.375
Chander?

00:08:10.417 --> 00:08:12.458
The Indore team wanted to know

00:08:12.542 --> 00:08:15.583
if you will be visiting next week
to finish the training.

00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:22.500
Sir, I was thinking of working
with the Bhopal team for a few days.

00:08:23.208 --> 00:08:25.375
I've got an idea.
Let's have Kartik attend the training.

00:08:25.458 --> 00:08:26.667
He'll take both the sessions.

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:31.792
For the first time in six months,
you've canceled a tour.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.083
It seems like the deal
is getting finalized.

00:08:35.917 --> 00:08:37.000
Okay.

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.625
- Enjoy your time together.
- Thank you.

00:08:42.333 --> 00:08:44.125
<i>But tell me, what does your heart say?</i>

00:08:44.208 --> 00:08:46.250
My heart is confused.

00:08:46.333 --> 00:08:47.292
Why?

00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:50.250
Either you like him, or you don't.

00:08:50.333 --> 00:08:52.458
- I like him.
- Yes?

00:08:52.542 --> 00:08:54.375
I like him a lot.

00:08:54.458 --> 00:08:55.500
And him?

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:57.167
What do you think?

00:08:57.250 --> 00:09:00.708
He's extremely caring and great company.

00:09:01.792 --> 00:09:03.042
You know, Gargi,

00:09:03.708 --> 00:09:08.125
around him, I feel like there's more
to me than just being a lawyer.

00:09:08.833 --> 00:09:10.333
Both things can happen, right?

00:09:12.542 --> 00:09:13.542
Give it some time.

00:09:14.042 --> 00:09:15.167
See where it goes.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.208
By the way, will Aunty like Chander?

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:21.583
Shut up!

00:09:21.667 --> 00:09:23.542
I bet you haven't told him
about this offer yet.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.333
Two days without me, and suddenly
you've grown so wise, Gargi!

00:09:28.417 --> 00:09:29.875
- Yeah. True.
- Wow!

00:09:34.917 --> 00:09:36.167
He's too cute.

00:09:41.042 --> 00:09:42.458
What are you doing here?

00:09:42.542 --> 00:09:44.542
I'm here to pick up my flatmate.

00:09:45.958 --> 00:09:47.458
Come, I'll introduce you to Gargi.

00:09:47.542 --> 00:09:49.167
Wait a minute.

00:09:51.417 --> 00:09:54.167
- Do you want to impress Gargi?
- Of course.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.667
The way to a girl's heart
is through her friend.

00:09:59.375 --> 00:10:00.417
Come on.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.208
- Hi, Chander!
- Hi, Gargi!

00:10:03.292 --> 00:10:06.083
- How are you?
- Absolutely fine. So good to see you.

00:10:06.167 --> 00:10:07.375
So good to see you also.

00:10:08.375 --> 00:10:11.667
I don't know if you know this,
but I'm Sudha's ex-flatmate

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.500
but permanent best friend.

00:10:15.083 --> 00:10:19.125
By the way, I've heard endless praise
about you and your tea.

00:10:20.292 --> 00:10:22.083
I've heard a lot of praise
about you as well.

00:10:22.167 --> 00:10:24.042
- About me? Really?
- Yes. Yes.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.917
Wow! You don't know how to lie either?

00:10:27.583 --> 00:10:28.458
Nice!

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.917
- Gargi!
- Okay, fine. Sorry.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.417
- I'll get going.
- Okay.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.750
- Bye, Gargi.
- Bye, Sudha.

00:10:34.833 --> 00:10:36.417
- Bye. Take care. See you soon.
- Bye.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.583
Take care, Sudha.

00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:42.958
Flatmate?

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:44.625
What else would I say?

00:10:46.042 --> 00:10:46.917
Wait a minute.

00:10:47.583 --> 00:10:49.417
Are we more than just flatmates?

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.792
Alright then, flatmate, what's the plan?

00:10:57.125 --> 00:10:58.417
Drink some water.

00:10:59.208 --> 00:11:01.792
- Who told you to order such spicy food?
- I knew it.

00:11:02.292 --> 00:11:03.917
Shall I get some sweet chutney?

00:11:07.792 --> 00:11:10.000
- Don't look there. Look here.
- Who is it?

00:11:11.083 --> 00:11:12.625
Chander. Chander.

00:11:12.708 --> 00:11:13.958
Chander, stop it! Stop it!

00:11:14.042 --> 00:11:16.667
That's the engineer from the cafe
who got rejected, right?

00:11:18.667 --> 00:11:19.583
<i>Bhaisahab!</i>

00:11:19.667 --> 00:11:21.667
<i>Bhaisahab!</i> Green T-shirt!

00:11:22.667 --> 00:11:23.583
Sudha!

00:11:28.708 --> 00:11:29.708
Hi, Kushal.

00:11:29.792 --> 00:11:30.917
Kushal. Hi!

00:11:35.042 --> 00:11:36.875
- Hey, Sudha, how are you?
- Hi.

00:11:37.667 --> 00:11:39.250
Meet Priya, my fiancée.

00:11:39.333 --> 00:11:41.458
- Priya, this is Sudha.
- I see.

00:11:42.667 --> 00:11:45.542
Wow, Kushal! Fiancée?

00:11:46.125 --> 00:11:47.708
Congratulations!

00:11:47.792 --> 00:11:49.375
Nice to meet you, Sudha.

00:11:49.458 --> 00:11:51.042
Nice to meet you, Priya.

00:11:57.417 --> 00:11:59.583
Chander Mohan Sharma,
my good friend.

00:12:02.458 --> 00:12:04.500
Oh, you were the one
at the cafe that day, right?

00:12:05.167 --> 00:12:06.042
Yes.

00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:08.167
By the way, my mom
spoke to your mom a few days ago.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.958
- How is she?
- Great. And your mom?

00:12:11.042 --> 00:12:12.667
- Very good.
- Good, good.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.000
How do you two know each other?

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:27.083
We met at a coffee shop.

00:12:27.583 --> 00:12:29.792
- Yes.
- We met at a coffee shop. Yes.

00:12:29.875 --> 00:12:32.708
But how do your mothers know each other?

00:12:36.583 --> 00:12:38.917
Well, it was Mother's Day.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.500
The cafe was running a "Bring one mom,
get another mom free" offer.

00:12:42.458 --> 00:12:44.625
Right. Shall we go for a milkshake?

00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:47.333
They have really good milkshakes, Priya.
Take a left from here.

00:12:47.417 --> 00:12:48.417
- Let's have a milkshake.
- Yes.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:49.458
- Yes.
- Best.

00:12:49.542 --> 00:12:50.417
Bye. Have fun.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:51.417
- Bye.
- Have fun.

00:12:57.083 --> 00:12:58.208
Mother's Day special?

00:12:59.625 --> 00:13:00.583
Good friend?

00:13:00.667 --> 00:13:02.667
Yes, what else could I say?

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:05.333
"This is Chander, my flatmate."

00:13:05.417 --> 00:13:08.625
He would've been scandalized enough
to call his mother in Ratlam,

00:13:08.708 --> 00:13:09.875
who would go on to call mine.

00:13:09.958 --> 00:13:11.125
Fair point.

00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:13.667
Well, he found a girl at record speed.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:16.000
Actually!
I was thinking the same thing.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.167
As soon as I rejected him,
he found his dream girl.

00:13:19.833 --> 00:13:23.000
I should get a commission-- Yuck!

00:13:23.083 --> 00:13:25.208
Is that how you eat<i> golgappas?</i>

00:13:26.292 --> 00:13:28.083
How does anyone eat <i>golgappas</i>
the wrong way?

00:13:28.167 --> 00:13:30.625
You're supposed to pop the whole thing
in your mouth in one go.

00:13:30.708 --> 00:13:33.125
- Oh!
- Didn't your girlfriend ever teach you?

00:13:37.667 --> 00:13:39.083
You had a girlfriend, right?

00:13:44.292 --> 00:13:45.333
Chander?

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.375
You had a girlfriend, right?

00:13:48.458 --> 00:13:50.333
Hey, stop saying "girlfriend"
all the time.

00:13:50.417 --> 00:13:51.833
I have a girlfriend.

00:13:53.083 --> 00:13:56.167
- What do you mean by "have"?
- "Have" means have!

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.875
- Where's she? Show me her photo.
- I don't have a photo.

00:13:58.958 --> 00:14:01.333
- It must be on your phone. Let me see!
- It's not on my phone.

00:14:01.417 --> 00:14:02.625
What do you mean
you have a girlfriend?

00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:05.250
You're sitting with me having <i>golgappas,</i>
and you've got a girlfriend?

00:14:05.333 --> 00:14:06.917
Hey, I'm talking about my ex!

00:14:08.583 --> 00:14:09.500
Ex.

00:14:09.583 --> 00:14:11.417
I just don't have the guts to say I had.

00:14:12.708 --> 00:14:13.833
Okay?

00:14:16.875 --> 00:14:19.167
- Did she like <i>golgappas?</i>
- Yes.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.542
A lot.

00:14:23.042 --> 00:14:25.083
Okay. Plan change.

00:14:26.917 --> 00:14:30.458
I can't tolerate emotional stories
without whiskey.

00:14:32.583 --> 00:14:33.500
So?

00:14:34.292 --> 00:14:35.500
College romance?

00:14:38.208 --> 00:14:39.375
Even older than that.

00:14:41.875 --> 00:14:46.208
Actually, back in Delhi,
her house was right next to mine.

00:14:46.917 --> 00:14:50.625
So, same school, same college.
We even did engineering together.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.417
Also, she got a US scholarship,

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.083
and I just went along for company.

00:14:56.833 --> 00:15:01.333
Just so I could keep her company,
my dad had to take a loan of 35 lakhs.

00:15:05.042 --> 00:15:06.000
I remember,

00:15:06.958 --> 00:15:10.250
before I left, he called me
into his room and said,

00:15:10.917 --> 00:15:14.250
"Chandu, you're going to America.
Work really hard."

00:15:16.167 --> 00:15:18.708
For the middle class,
even dreams are bought on EMI.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.583
Anyway…

00:15:22.792 --> 00:15:25.875
So, one day, my girlfriend met Chris.

00:15:27.208 --> 00:15:29.833
She broke up with me
over a long-distance phone call.

00:15:31.083 --> 00:15:34.500
Our childhood love didn't make it
from the East Coast to the West Coast.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.125
Then I worked really hard there
for two years.

00:15:40.208 --> 00:15:42.792
I used to work,
but my heart was never really in it.

00:15:43.625 --> 00:15:46.042
One night, while having
a couple of drinks,

00:15:46.125 --> 00:15:48.333
I told myself,
"Enough. I'm going back home."

00:15:50.083 --> 00:15:51.250
So, I came home.

00:15:51.333 --> 00:15:55.333
But the welcome I got from my family
and neighbors was filled with sadness.

00:15:55.417 --> 00:15:58.250
Mom didn't even understand
what had happened to me there.

00:15:58.875 --> 00:16:00.125
And Dad just

00:16:00.958 --> 00:16:02.917
placed the loan documents on the table.

00:16:05.375 --> 00:16:08.125
I think he was really disappointed in me.

00:16:09.542 --> 00:16:10.500
But…

00:16:12.208 --> 00:16:14.875
I paid off the entire student loan.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:25.083
Last year, I found out
she had married someone else.

00:16:25.167 --> 00:16:27.167
She lives in Singapore. She's happy.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.875
And ever since then, Mom's been after me.
"Marriage, marriage, marriage."

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.333
Well, that's my story.

00:16:36.125 --> 00:16:37.000
The end.

00:16:37.083 --> 00:16:38.292
Cheers!

00:16:39.417 --> 00:16:40.500
Bottoms up.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:49.875
Ice?

00:17:00.167 --> 00:17:02.500
One more question.
And tell me the truth, okay?

00:17:03.875 --> 00:17:04.792
Did you cry?

00:17:07.958 --> 00:17:08.917
A lot.

00:17:10.542 --> 00:17:11.583
But in solitude.

00:17:12.292 --> 00:17:14.250
I couldn't cry in front of Mom and Dad.

00:17:15.333 --> 00:17:16.708
That's why, Bhopal.

00:17:18.167 --> 00:17:19.458
<i>Don't you find it weird?</i>

00:17:19.542 --> 00:17:21.375
<i>A grown-up man wanting to cry?</i>

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:23.875
Not at all.

00:17:25.083 --> 00:17:29.167
In fact, it's the most sensible thing
I've heard today.

00:17:29.792 --> 00:17:31.208
Because at least you do cry.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.250
What about those who can't even cry
when they're supposed to?

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.625
Those who can't even process it.

00:17:42.125 --> 00:17:43.292
May I ask you something?

00:17:44.667 --> 00:17:46.500
Why don't you want to get married?

00:17:46.583 --> 00:17:50.085
You know everything about me now.
Tell me something about yourself as well.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:56.792
When Dad was around, I had big dreams.

00:17:58.708 --> 00:18:03.792
When I used to tell him that I wanted
to go to Oxford University to study law,

00:18:04.667 --> 00:18:05.708
he would say…

00:18:06.833 --> 00:18:07.792
"Sudhbudh!"

00:18:08.667 --> 00:18:12.042
"Just score good marks, and I'll arrange
your visa tomorrow myself!"

00:18:14.958 --> 00:18:15.917
But you know,

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:20.000
I've always held on to something
Dad once told me.

00:18:21.583 --> 00:18:23.583
I always worked very hard,

00:18:24.167 --> 00:18:27.042
scored good marks,
and topped the class.

00:18:28.667 --> 00:18:30.042
I couldn't go to Oxford,

00:18:30.875 --> 00:18:34.500
but I did manage to get out of Ratlam
and come to Bhopal District Court.

00:18:39.167 --> 00:18:40.375
After coming here,

00:18:40.917 --> 00:18:45.042
I learned what it truly means
to stand on my own two feet.

00:18:48.625 --> 00:18:50.208
I can't stop now, Chander.

00:18:52.667 --> 00:18:54.250
I want to achieve more in life.

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:58.958
But don't you ever feel lonely?

00:19:00.458 --> 00:19:03.625
Loneliness can also be cured
with alcohol and friends.

00:19:06.458 --> 00:19:08.167
It can also be a partner

00:19:09.833 --> 00:19:12.542
who truly accepts me.

00:19:19.583 --> 00:19:20.625
And boyfriends?

00:19:21.917 --> 00:19:23.167
Of course, I've had them.

00:19:23.958 --> 00:19:26.583
But eventually,
marriage and kids find their way

00:19:26.667 --> 00:19:28.917
into their plans
or their family's expectations.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.750
They just can't accept me the way I am.

00:19:31.833 --> 00:19:35.917
So, they come and they go.
And I say, "Thank you. Goodbye."

00:19:39.042 --> 00:19:43.083
Anyway,
I've never really been in true love.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.083
Never happened,
or you never let it happen?

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:47.625
Both.

00:19:48.375 --> 00:19:52.917
And from now on, never have
emotional drunk conversations with me.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:53.917
Why?

00:19:54.583 --> 00:19:58.667
Because now, even in Bhopal,
you'll get less privacy to cry.

00:20:01.792 --> 00:20:04.875
Oh, as if you're going to stay in Bhopal.

00:20:05.917 --> 00:20:07.625
You're going to Mumbai.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.250
What did you say?

00:20:14.333 --> 00:20:15.833
So, when are you going?

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:18.625
I'm thinking about it.

00:20:19.583 --> 00:20:21.708
Okay. I'm really sorry.

00:20:21.792 --> 00:20:25.125
I accidentally saw your offer letter.
It was lying on the study table.

00:20:25.208 --> 00:20:27.208
Please don't take this the wrong way.

00:20:27.292 --> 00:20:32.625
And I understand what a huge leap
this could be for you and your career.

00:20:33.292 --> 00:20:34.250
And…

00:20:34.917 --> 00:20:38.292
Look, with all this happening,
I forgot to congratulate you.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:41.750
Congratulations.

00:20:43.042 --> 00:20:46.250
Why are you even thinking about it?
Just go for it.

00:20:46.333 --> 00:20:48.958
You won't feel bad if I leave?

00:20:50.208 --> 00:20:51.125
Well…

00:20:51.792 --> 00:20:52.667
I…

00:20:57.625 --> 00:21:01.333
By the way,
I need to confess something too.

00:21:04.042 --> 00:21:08.875
When you weren't here, I found
something other than whiskey.

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:10.375
What?

00:21:17.792 --> 00:21:19.667
Is the cafe plan serious or just…?

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:28.417
You know,
this is the only real dream I have.

00:21:30.417 --> 00:21:34.417
You know, there used to be
this quaint little bookstore in Old Delhi

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.208
with a coffee shop inside.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:40.750
My grandpa used to sit there for hours.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:45.875
And everyone who passed by
would always stop to chat with my grandpa.

00:21:45.958 --> 00:21:48.083
I don't know what
because I was too young at that time.

00:21:48.167 --> 00:21:50.417
I was ten, eleven, maybe.

00:21:52.292 --> 00:21:55.917
But I do know that Grandpa had
a different connection with that place.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.083
He was really happy there.

00:22:01.542 --> 00:22:02.458
Beautiful.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.208
You know, how easy it is
to talk to strangers

00:22:05.292 --> 00:22:06.958
when they know nothing about you.

00:22:08.625 --> 00:22:12.042
I want to create that kind of experience
in my dream cafe.

00:22:14.833 --> 00:22:18.208
Anyway, now you know
what a great host I am. So…

00:22:20.542 --> 00:22:22.000
The best.

00:22:24.625 --> 00:22:26.750
I've made a small change here.

00:22:27.542 --> 00:22:28.833
Hope you don't mind.

00:22:35.417 --> 00:22:36.417
Musafir.

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:40.833
Musafir.

00:22:58.208 --> 00:23:00.250
Three, two, one.

00:23:00.333 --> 00:23:04.500
Hey, guys! I'm here at the Musafir Cafe.
And guess who I have with me here?

00:23:04.583 --> 00:23:07.833
The founders themselves,
Chander and Preeti.

00:23:07.917 --> 00:23:10.792
Well, this is a beautiful space
you guys have created.

00:23:10.875 --> 00:23:12.042
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:23:12.125 --> 00:23:15.708
Tell me, how did you come up
with the name "Musafir Cafe"?

00:23:17.667 --> 00:23:20.667
Actually, someone gifted me this name
many years ago.

00:23:21.333 --> 00:23:24.167
When this cafe was just a small dream.

00:23:24.708 --> 00:23:28.292
Wow. And what about
this famous promise wall?

00:23:28.375 --> 00:23:30.417
Tell us what makes it so special.

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:34.750
So, we believe every traveler,
every <i>musafir, </i>has a purpose.

00:23:34.833 --> 00:23:37.958
And if that purpose is fulfilled
through a journey,

00:23:38.042 --> 00:23:39.958
then that experience
becomes memorable, no?

00:23:40.042 --> 00:23:41.042
Yeah.

00:23:41.125 --> 00:23:43.583
So, this promise wall
is filled with people's journeys

00:23:43.667 --> 00:23:46.292
and promises that they make to themselves.

00:23:46.375 --> 00:23:48.667
So, people come, they write,
and they put it on the wall.

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:49.708
And…

00:23:49.792 --> 00:23:52.167
If they ever return here,

00:23:52.250 --> 00:23:54.083
they'll find
all their promises right here.

00:23:54.167 --> 00:23:55.167
That I can promise.

00:23:55.250 --> 00:23:57.250
Well, that's a beautiful thought.

00:23:57.333 --> 00:24:00.458
Also, I was talking to Rahil Qureshi,
the author,

00:24:00.542 --> 00:24:03.750
and he said that if Chander
is the foundation of this cafe,

00:24:03.833 --> 00:24:06.792
then Preeti is the heart
that keeps the artists going.

00:24:06.875 --> 00:24:07.833
Where did you two meet?

00:24:07.917 --> 00:24:09.792
How did this partnership begin?

00:24:11.792 --> 00:24:12.917
- Tell her.
- Five years ago…

00:24:13.958 --> 00:24:16.708
I boarded the wrong bus
on my way to Rishikesh.

00:24:16.792 --> 00:24:20.500
And at 9:00 p.m., she was asking
for an address at a tea stall.

00:24:20.583 --> 00:24:22.417
What was the name of that place?

00:24:22.500 --> 00:24:24.167
- Cloud and View Home Stay.
- Cloud and View Home Stay.

00:24:24.250 --> 00:24:25.125
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:24:25.208 --> 00:24:27.000
Which had actually shut down
six months ago.

00:24:27.083 --> 00:24:28.625
- And she didn't know about that.
- Yeah.

00:24:28.708 --> 00:24:31.375
So, we ended up
spending the night talking,

00:24:31.458 --> 00:24:34.083
and realized how similar
our dreams were.

00:24:34.167 --> 00:24:36.125
Oh my God.
Such a sweet love story.

00:24:36.208 --> 00:24:38.583
Also, how long have you been married?

00:24:40.708 --> 00:24:42.708
Like you said, we are partners.

00:24:43.208 --> 00:24:45.250
In life, in business,

00:24:45.917 --> 00:24:47.000
and in dreams.

00:24:48.625 --> 00:24:50.000
Alright, well…

00:24:50.083 --> 00:24:53.417
I can't wait for all my viewers
to come to Musafir Cafe

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:56.583
and enjoy this vibe and energy
you guys have created.

00:24:56.667 --> 00:24:58.125
Thank you so much for chatting with me.

00:24:58.208 --> 00:25:01.250
- Thank you, Preeti. Thank you, Chander.
- Thank you.

00:25:17.667 --> 00:25:19.792
<i>Thank you, Dubey sir,</i>
<i>for this opportunity.</i>

00:25:20.375 --> 00:25:22.458
<i>But I need some time.</i>

00:25:23.208 --> 00:25:24.833
<i>For now, can we put this on hold?</i>

00:25:25.625 --> 00:25:28.167
<i>I want to spend some more time</i>
<i>here in Bhopal.</i>

00:25:28.667 --> 00:25:33.875
<i>Day after day</i>
<i>You find your way into my heart</i>

00:25:33.958 --> 00:25:38.750
<i>You understand the silence I hide within</i>

00:25:40.042 --> 00:25:45.208
<i>A gentle peace comes over me</i>
<i>Whenever you're near</i>

00:25:45.708 --> 00:25:50.208
{\an8}<i>Even my breath seems to stand still…</i>

00:25:50.792 --> 00:25:55.250
{\an8}<i>Mumbai will have to wait, Gargi.</i>
<i>I'm trying love for a change.</i>

00:25:57.167 --> 00:26:00.917
<i>I whispered a prayer to the falling stars</i>

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:06.333
<i>I've become yours, my love</i>

00:26:06.917 --> 00:26:12.083
<i>I've become yours, my love</i>

00:26:12.583 --> 00:26:18.625
<i>I've given myself to you</i>

00:26:18.708 --> 00:26:23.333
<i>My love</i>

00:28:53.625 --> 00:28:55.625
Subtitle translation by: Neha Nair


